From a0c3e14efdd6a5d8c03652f83f563ec6210dd541 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: primez <mpincoski@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 09:32:15 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] [ADTSReader] Seek HLS packed audio to the target, and read
 AC-3 and E-AC-3 frames whole

Backport the ADTS part of upstream e727bae22d and e15a188da0, and fix the
AC-3/E-AC-3 frame reads of the ADTS reader. The ADTS tests build as a
separate executable with a memory stream that can wait for a live segment.

- Fix HLS audio starting before video after a seek, which froze the
  picture on Amlogic
- Fix the timestamps of stereo AC-3 and of E-AC-3 frames with fewer than
  6 blocks in HLS audio
- Fix a seek in a live HLS stream that ended the audio when the next
  audio segment was not available yet
- Fix the timestamps of 7.1 channel E-AC-3 HLS audio, and send both
  substreams of a frame as one sample
- Fix the timing offset of HLS audio after each segment change, which
  was one frame wrong until the next seek

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
